course: dictionary
lesson: 14587
title: Pleasers and crowd-pleasers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pleaser is a person or thing that pleases others. The word comes from the verb please, and the ending -er shows the person or thing that does it.
explain: «Maya is a people-pleaser. She says yes to every request, even when she is tired.» A people-pleaser always tries to make others happy and finds it hard to say no, even when it is bad for them.
explain: «The new cake was a crowd-pleaser at the school fair.» A crowd-pleaser is something that lots of people enjoy. Check it by swapping in your meaning: a cake that many people enjoy still makes sense here.
fact: Pleaser is a noun: a pleaser, pleasers.
fact: «Pleaser» means a person or thing that pleases others.
fact: «People-pleaser» means someone who tries to make others happy, even when it is bad for themselves.
fact: «Crowd-pleaser» means something that lots of people enjoy, like a popular song, film or dish.
fact: It is fine to say no politely, even when you want to make everyone happy.
exercise: «Maya always says yes, even when she is tired. She is a people-pleaser.» What is a people-pleaser? | Someone who never plays with other children | Someone who is always late for school | *Someone who tries to make others happy, even when it is bad for them | A person who sings very loudly
exercise: «The new song was a crowd-pleaser at the party.» What does crowd-pleaser mean here? | *Something lots of people enjoy | A very small room | A noisy dog that barks at everyone | Something that makes a crowd run away
exercise: Ruby is asked to do extra homework every night. The wellbeing lesson says what is fine? | To always agree, even when you are tired | To hide your own feelings | *To say no politely | To never speak up at all
test: «Sam is a people-pleaser who finds it hard to say no.» What does people-pleaser mean? | Someone who never tries to make others happy | A person who plays football | Someone who likes to be alone | *Someone who tries to make others happy, even when it is bad for themselves
test: Which of these is a crowd-pleaser? | A quiet book read alone in bed | Homework that takes all evening | *A popular song that everyone at the party sings along to | A cold, empty room
exam: Which word is a noun meaning a person or thing that pleases others? | pleased | pleasing | *pleaser | pleasant
